This is possible without adding extra configuration or environment variables. In the setup function, you can use a custom provider to run any script you want. For example, you can use a script that works like the `opencode run` like this:

```lua
return {
  "ThePrimeagen/99",
  config = function()
    local _99 = require("99")

    ---@class BashProvider: OpenCodeProvider
    local BashProvider = setmetatable({}, { __index = _99.Providers.OpenCodeProvider })
    function BashProvider._build_command(_, query, request)
      return { "/tmp/my-bash-script", query }
    end

    _99.setup({
      -- ...
      provider = BashProvider,
      -- ...
    })
  end,
}
```

